    "bodySha256": "6df9e906d3c3ce0589cd1627b2bb89215982ecfab87add6345d9fc02b15615f1",
    "body": "# omp-spec-kit v1.4.0\n\n## Included changes\n\n- Promotes the bounded 10-tool MCP surface to the stable major release: 9 read-only tools and one transactional `spec_patch` authoring tool.\n- Preserves bounded entity, graph, document, evidence, and Markdown queries with pagination, projections, cursors, and traversal limits.\n- Verifies the complete semantic tool-E2E matrix against the built server and the exact release archive launcher.\n\n## Verified release\n\n- Candidate digest: `0e9bf9570b755e09ebd514c8a357a4f92e07809809bc3c6fe2c72b56f2dec266`\n- Package tree digest: `1a3a2f25edd7673243b494a67cba6222ff449cfbc757d6202f5fddb7f16da817`\n- Archive SHA-256: `377aa6c739b967200b860e417497b4812308fc50b1460b9bfcce7149350c90d9`\n- Peeled tag commit: `87a00412fd9e7146580864eb62de9b3fc5c8ab63`\n- OMP runtime: `18.0.11`\n- Distribution evidence: lifecycle producers, Docker BDD, manager discovery, and nine closed MRI receipts.\n\nInstall or upgrade at project scope, reload plugin metadata, then start a fresh OMP session before invoking MCP tools.\n\n"
